findings:
- **HIGH — Push binding is not enforced at execution.** Judgment correctly binds operands to the carried row (`extended.rs:1141-1157`), but execution discards that row (`extended.rs:1915`) and `bridge_execute` only checks data shapes (`extended.rs:439-454`). A caller of the public execution helper can supply a registered PSH1 row with operands/result types outside that row.
- **HIGH — `Index` code 2 is not a valid typed constant end-to-end.** E8 constructs `BuiltinFailure(Index, 2)` (`extended.rs:385-393`), while `TypeEnvironment::check_constant` permits only code 1 for `Index` (`crates/sley-check/src/lib.rs:1067-1074`). Report projection validates constants (`sley-conformance/src/lib.rs:803-810`), so the advertised capacity failure cannot remain a valid canonical result through reporting.
